From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: keep the FS primitive ID across VS viewport runs
 biblioklept

A VS that writes ViewportIndex is drawn as one IDVS draw per viewport
run, and the hardware primitive ID restarts at each run (and did not
restart per instance, the run list flattens instances). When the FS
reads PrimitiveID and the VS has no PrimitiveID output, the run builder
packs the primitive ID (per instance, across restarts, plus the CPU
chunk's primitive base) into index bits 16+; the vp passthrough reads
the record from bits 0-15 and outputs PrimitiveID, which the tiler
uses through primitive_index_override. Run draws have restart off. TES
already outputs its patch ID and is unchanged. Host test extended.

Generated-by: LLM
